# E-1005: Let $\frac{a_1}{b_1},\frac{a_2}{b_2},\ldots$ be the Farey fractions of order $n\geq 4$. Let $f(n)$ be the largest integer such that if $1\leq k<l\leq k+f(n)$ then $\frac{a_k}{b_k}$ and $\frac{a_l}{b_l}$ are similarly ordered - in other words,\[(a_k-a_l)(b_k-b_l)\geq 0.\]Estimate $f(n)$ - in particular, is there a constant $c>0$ such that $f(n)=(c+o(1))n$ for all large $n$?
